# Local CI before release tag

**Never** create or push `release/X.Y.Z` until latest `origin/main` passed `bash scripts/ci/run-release-tag-local-ci.sh`. A green prep PR is **not** a substitute — PR Typecheck can skip `eslint .`. Release **always** runs it.

```bash
git fetch origin main && git checkout main && git pull origin main
bash scripts/ci/run-release-tag-local-ci.sh
git tag release/X.Y.Z
git push origin refs/tags/release/X.Y.Z
```

**Lessons:** 0.8.1 lint skip; **0.9.6** unused import after tagging from green Integration tests. `ci:verify:release-ts` ETARGET before npm is expected — do not skip the three required steps. Workspace hook denies tag/push without the stamp file.

See [`scripts/RELEASE.md`](../../scripts/RELEASE.md).
